[hheller@charlesriver.East.Sun.COM asks:]
>How do you kill something that divides everytime you hit it?
>Do you have to have wands around to zap it with or something?
.
every time you hit a pudding you do damage! if the original pudding
started with 40 Hp's and you hit for 5 damage, you'll now see two
puddings, each with 35 Hp's. if you keep hitting them they will
eventually die. killing them in 1 move is an effective strategy
if you have the right magic. you can keep the puddings from attacking
you by writing the magic word "Elbereth". if your spelling is correct
and the word is intact, you're safe ...
.
>Also, sometimes when I wish for things, I wish for the wrong name
>of the thing and get something else (blessed potion of
>Restore Strength is an example that comes to mind.) What are the
>rules on wishing? I know you can wish for up to 3 of the item,
>you can make it "blessed", any other 'modifiers' allowed? Does
>someone have a list of the 'things' you can wish for (eg; their
>exact names that nethack understands)?
.
a successful wish places an item into your inventory. to wish
effectively, you should wish for an item that can (literally) be placed
in your inventory. you could wish for a wide sword and get one. better
yet, you could wish for a +3 wide sword and you would at least get a
wide sword. whether you get the asked for enchantments depends on a
random factor that is in part, i believe, based on your luck. you may
wish for enchantments as high as +5. this is an all or nothing
proposition and the chances of getting higher enchantments are worse
than lower enchantments so you're better off wishing for +2 grey dragon
scale mail than let's say +4 black dragon scale mail. in either case
you'll get at least +0 <color> dragon scale mail with the odds in your
favor for getting the +2 variety. the general modifiers are, of course,
blessed, uncursed and cursed. a specific modifier for small missile
weapons is poisoned (as it appears in your inventory). also there are
named weapons, as in a blessed +3 wide sword named Stormbringer. in no
particular order here's a few nice wishes (possible in nh3.0f3 at least):
blessed +3 wide sword named Stormbringer
blessed +3 samarai sword named Snickersnee
blessed +3 long sword named Excalibur
blessed +3 athame
blessed +3 grey dragon scale mail
blessed +3 helm of telepathy
blessed +3 pair of speed boots
blessed +3 gauntlets of power
blessed +3 shield of reflection
blessed +3 cloak of protection
blessed +3 hawaiian shirt
3 blessed potions of gain level
3 blessed potions of gain ability
a blessed potion of invisibility
a blessed potion of see invisible
3 blessed scrolls of genocide
3 cursed scrolls of genocide ... caution is advised!
3 blessed spellbooks of identify
3 blessed spellbooks of polymorph
3 blessed spellbooks of cancellation
3 blessed spellbooks of cure sickness
a blessed amulet of life saving
a blessed ring of polymorph control
a blessed ring of levitation
a wand of polymorph

this list is far from optimal but there's enough here for you to do
damage to a fair amount of the dungeon ... fare thee well.

